---
import model from '../ml/model.json';

const { training } = model;
---
<section class="section" id="status">
  <p class="eyebrow">08 / Project status</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Built to explore. Clear about its limits.</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">The software is running. The hardware is a design proposal. Here is where the project stands.</p>

  <div class="status">
    <div class="status-col">
      <h3>Proposed</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The wristband and its component layout, shown here as concept renders and design studies.</li>
        <li>The onboard server built around a Raspberry Pi, and its hand-off to spacecraft communications.</li>
        <li>A model trained on each astronaut's measured reference sessions.</li>
        <li>Motion and multispectral channels as model inputs. Whether they help is untested.</li>
        <li>Spectra Link on real network standards: Bundle Protocol, bundle security and a fountain code.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="status-col">
      <h3>Running today</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The interactive demo in your browser, on synthetic data.</li>
        <li>A neural network of {training.parameters} parameters, trained on {training.sessions} synthetic sessions.</li>
        <li>A statistical baseline beside it, and an evaluation on held-out synthetic sessions.</li>
        <li>Crew monitors with a trend warning, a likely cause and incident grouping, all rule-based.</li>
        <li>A simulated link with real light time and solar blackouts, priorities, packet loss and a verifiable event log.</li>
        <li>A ground copy of the reference model that receives only what it could not predict.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
